<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Klia		 unloading   corn	     33,872     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,432</p>
<p>				     soya	     11,953</p>
<p>				     wheat	     8,827</p>
<p>Matushenko	 arrived     maize grits     2,858     Europe</p>
<p>Omsky 139	  arrived     feed wheat	2,741     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 233     arrived     feed wheat	2,882     Europe</p>
<p>Baltisky 55	arrived     feed wheat	2,029     Europe</p>
<p>Baltisky 69	arrived     feed wheat	1,931     Europe</p>
<p>Coot		  7/4	  sunflower	 2,923</p>
<p>Busteni	     8/4	  rapeseed meal   7,000     India</p>
<p>Orel 4		9/4	  sunflower	 1,840     Europe</p>
<p>Southern Venture 10/4	  corn	     25,657     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     17,700</p>
<p>Ivan Kudria	12/4	  maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Geroi Arsenala    n/a	  sunflower meal  2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Omsky 138	  15/4	  maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Volgodon 5039    16/4	  feed wheat	3,614     Europe</p>
<p>Evangolos	  17/4	  sorghum	  35,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Matheos	    18/4	  corn	     20,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  15,000</p>
<p>				     barley	   15,000</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	25/4	  wheat+sorghum+ 60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					 soya</p>
